From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:04:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chunkio: take byte-order helpers from gulliver.h on QNX

The bundled crc32 code needs htole16(), le16toh(), htobe16(), be16toh() and
__BYTE_ORDER. The QNX SDP 8.0 has neither <endian.h> nor <sys/endian.h>.
Its byte-order helpers are ENDIAN_LE16() and ENDIAN_BE16() in <gulliver.h>,
selected by __LITTLEENDIAN__ or __BIGENDIAN__.

Add a QNX branch that maps the missing names onto the gulliver.h macros and
defines __BYTE_ORDER from __BIGENDIAN__.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 lib/chunkio/deps/crc32/crc32.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/chunkio/deps/crc32/crc32.c b/lib/chunkio/deps/crc32/crc32.c
index 58b3912..f38388e 100644
--- a/lib/chunkio/deps/crc32/crc32.c
+++ b/lib/chunkio/deps/crc32/crc32.c
@@ -51,6 +51,19 @@
 #   define BYTE_ORDER LITTLE_ENDIAN
 #  endif
 # endif
+#elif defined(__QNXNTO__)
+#  include <gulliver.h>
+#  define htole16(x) ENDIAN_LE16(x)
+#  define le16toh(x) ENDIAN_LE16(x)
+#  define htobe16(x) ENDIAN_BE16(x)
+#  define be16toh(x) ENDIAN_BE16(x)
+#  define __BIG_ENDIAN 4321
+#  define __LITTLE_ENDIAN 1234
+#  if defined(__BIGENDIAN__)
+#    define __BYTE_ORDER __BIG_ENDIAN
+#  else
+#    define __BYTE_ORDER __LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#  endif
 #else
 #  include <endian.h>
 #endif
